Constraints {
  The model's assigned review covers cryptography, key management and protocol security.
  Requested findings concern attacker-exploitable mathematics or protocol negotiation.
  if (the only evidence is generic MD5 hygiene) { The model is asked to omit that candidate. }
  The repeated mathematics/protocol-negotiation exclusion at source lines 28–29 remains a repeated instruction, not an extra review phase.
  Initial search priorities are non-exhaustive; the model is asked to reason beyond them.
  if (secret/HMAC/token equality uses ==, equals or memcmp) {
    The model is asked to examine early-exit timing disclosure against constant-time comparison.
  }
  if (JWT/signature verification trusts the token's algorithm or key id) {
    The requested checks include alg=none, HS/RS confusion and kid path traversal.
  }
  if (an encryption IV/nonce is constant, predictable or derived from replayable input) {
    The requested analysis includes GCM nonce-reuse authenticity compromise.
  }
  The model is asked to inspect non-CSPRNG token/IV/key/OTP/reset-code generation, including Math.random, rand(), Random() and random.random.
  The requested verification checks distinguish configured TLS/signature verification from actual enforcement: empty trust managers, always-true hostname checks and ignored verification results.
  Requested inspection includes literal keys/salts/passphrases in source or config, and key material exposed through logs/errors.
}

Constraints {
  The model acts as an authorization reviewer seeking absent or incorrect object, tenant and role checks.
  Before reporting, its evidence must identify the authenticating entry point/principal and the specific acted-on resource's ownership/tenant/role check location.
  if (that object-specific check exists and is correct) { The requested disposition is to drop the candidate. }
  Login alone is not accepted as proof of object authorization.
  if (the target is fixed/hardcoded rather than request-varied) {
    The model is asked to bound the issue to that record; do not label it arbitrary IDOR/BOLA.
  }
  Requested search includes every externally reachable handler, direct object/path/S3 references, asymmetric sibling/service guards, vertical escalation, mass-assignment of security fields, tenant-blind queries/caches and destructive unscoped bulk operations.
  Unscoped destructive bulk operations are requested as first-class high-impact findings.
  Search examples are non-exhaustive; in-depth confirmation remains model analysis, not a deterministic host check.
}

Constraints {
  The requested attacker model is an upstream producer, scheduler/operator parameter or shared landing-directory writer, not an interactive web user.
  A requested finding must cite an externally influenced job/env/record/filename value and the file:line where unvalidated data reaches a path, command, SQL or output record.
  if (producer and consumer share one trust domain and no lower-privileged party can set the value) { The model is asked to drop it. }
  Requested analysis covers canonical base-directory confinement, record-derived path collisions, planted/newest files and TOCTOU, COMP-3/EBCDIC length/sign/zone validation and COBOL/Python indexing differences, trailer counts/hash totals, CSV formula prefixes = + - @, shell/tool arguments, and writable restart/checkpoint state causing double posting.
  The search list is non-exhaustive; no precise exploitability cutoff is added.
}

Constraints {
